We all own the whole code, we share responsibility, if there is an error somewhere, 
that is the concern for all of us.

When someone finds an error, he/she treats it as its own error and tries to resolve the 
problem. We never follow the scheme: "this is your error, you must correct the code,
I don't care". 

However, every module has its owner - the module's owner is the person that knows
the module the best of us. Every correction to the module HAS TO BE APPROVED by the 
module's owner. BEFORE commiting any changes to repo, EVERYONE IS OBLIGED to consult
the changes with the module's owner.

The owner of the module should be willing to help anyone with bugs, modifications
and extensions in its module. However we adopt the rule:

EVERY BUG IN THE CODE IS MY BUG. EVERY SUCCESS IS THE SUCCESS OF ALL OF US.

